blackbox: add x86 system adapter

The OpenHarmony blackbox core (drivers/staging/blackbox) is only a registry
of modules; panic is caught by a platform system adapter. OpenHarmony ships
one only for Rockchip (drivers/staging/blackbox/rockchip, added by
kernel/linux/patches/linux-6.6/rk3568_patch/kernel.patch, under
ARCH_ROCKCHIP).

Add an x86 copy of rockchip/system_adapter.c (pstore ram variant). The code
is platform independent except the data cache flush before reboot:
dcache_clean_inval_poc(), __flush_dcache_area() and
__cpuc_flush_dcache_area() exist only on ARM; on x86 use
clflush_cache_range().

The hooks are placed at the top of blackbox/Kconfig and blackbox/Makefile,
so the patch applies both to the plain kernel_linux_6.6 tree and on top of
rk3568_patch, which appends its lines to the end of these files. Link order
does not matter: the core uses a static ops_list and core_initcall, the
adapter postcore_initcall.

Requires CONFIG_PSTORE, CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM, CONFIG_PSTORE_BLACKBOX and
CONFIG_BLACKBOX_STORAGE_BY_PSTORE_RAM. Not tested on hardware yet.

